msgid "Follow Windows display settings"
msgstr "Follow Windows display settings"

msgid "Safety-first default for new users. It offers fewer operations, which lowers the risk of an unintended change. Choose it while learning or when you only need to open and inspect models, manage jobs, run careful single-point checks, or search manuals."
msgstr "Safety-first default for new users. It offers fewer operations, which lowers the risk of an unintended change. Choose it while learning or when you only need to open and inspect models, manage jobs, run careful single-point checks, or search manuals."

msgid "Recommended for most users. It covers ordinary FEM model building and result export, and includes tools for making a Windows standalone package. Choose it for general simulation work that does not need a specialist profile."
msgstr "Recommended for most users. It covers ordinary FEM model building and result export, and includes tools for making a Windows standalone package. Choose it for general simulation work that does not need a specialist profile."

msgid "For optical and metasurface work. Adds materials, field review, Wave Optics checks, point audits, and staged parameter workflows to Core."
msgstr "For optical and metasurface work. Adds materials, field review, Wave Optics checks, point audits, and staged parameter workflows to Core."

msgid "For testing extra helpers that are broader or less mature. Use it only when a required tool is missing from the safer profiles, and check every output carefully."
msgstr "For testing extra helpers that are broader or less mature. Use it only when a required tool is missing from the safer profiles, and check every output carefully."

msgid "For old workflows that need nearly every tool. It keeps older broad path behavior and has weaker file containment. New users should not choose it."
msgstr "For old workflows that need nearly every tool. It keeps older broad path behavior and has weaker file containment. New users should not choose it."

msgid "Folder for working files and locks. Use an ASCII-only path. \nExample: %PROGRAMDATA%\\comsol_mcp\\runtime"
msgstr "Folder for working files and locks. Use an ASCII-only path. \nExample: %PROGRAMDATA%\\comsol_mcp\\runtime"

msgid "Optional separate folder for resumable jobs. Leave it empty to use the runtime folder. \nExample: %PROGRAMDATA%\\comsol_mcp\\runtime\\jobs"
msgstr "Optional separate folder for resumable jobs. Leave it empty to use the runtime folder. \nExample: %PROGRAMDATA%\\comsol_mcp\\runtime\\jobs"

msgid "Folders where COMSOL MCP may read your .mph files. Chinese paths are supported. \nExample: %LOCALAPPDATA%\\comsol_mcp\\models"
msgstr "Folders where COMSOL MCP may read your .mph files. Chinese paths are supported. \nExample: %LOCALAPPDATA%\\comsol_mcp\\models"

msgid "Folder where COMSOL MCP writes results and evidence. Use an ASCII-only path. \nExample: %PROGRAMDATA%\\comsol_mcp\\artifacts"
msgstr "Folder where COMSOL MCP writes results and evidence. Use an ASCII-only path. \nExample: %PROGRAMDATA%\\comsol_mcp\\artifacts"

msgid "Folder where COMSOL Multiphysics 6.4 is installed. \nExample: C:\\COMSOL64\\Multiphysics"
msgstr "Folder where COMSOL Multiphysics 6.4 is installed. \nExample: C:\\COMSOL64\\Multiphysics"

msgid "Java folder used by COMSOL. Auto-detect can fill this value. \nExample: C:\\COMSOL64\\Multiphysics\\java\\win64\\jre"
msgstr "Java folder used by COMSOL. Auto-detect can fill this value. \nExample: C:\\COMSOL64\\Multiphysics\\java\\win64\\jre"

msgid "JDK folder used by COMSOL. Auto-detect can fill this value. \nExample: C:\\COMSOL64\\Multiphysics\\java\\win64\\jre"
msgstr "JDK folder used by COMSOL. Auto-detect can fill this value. \nExample: C:\\COMSOL64\\Multiphysics\\java\\win64\\jre"

msgid "Enable optional interactive collaboration with a COMSOL Desktop connected to a local Server. This feature composes with every tool profile."
msgstr "Enable optional interactive collaboration with a COMSOL Desktop connected to a local Server. This feature composes with every tool profile."

msgid "Check that execution results and scientific conclusions are reported separately."
msgstr "Check that execution results and scientific conclusions are reported separately."

msgid "Check saved result files and their hashes."
msgstr "Check saved result files and their hashes."

msgid "Check that summary statements match the saved result values."
msgstr "Check that summary statements match the saved result values."

msgid "Check that a resumed job uses the same producer and driver."
msgstr "Check that a resumed job uses the same producer and driver."

msgid "Enable optional semantic manual-search tools for the selected profile. This feature requires prepared local indexes and a search model."
msgstr "Enable optional semantic manual-search tools for the selected profile. This feature requires prepared local indexes and a search model."

msgid "Optional folder containing prepared semantic-search files. This is not COMSOL's built-in manual folder. \nExample: %LOCALAPPDATA%\\comsol_mcp\\semantic\\manuals"
msgstr "Optional folder containing prepared semantic-search files. This is not COMSOL's built-in manual folder. \nExample: %LOCALAPPDATA%\\comsol_mcp\\semantic\\manuals"

msgid "Optional SQLite file used for manual text search. \nExample: %LOCALAPPDATA%\\comsol_mcp\\semantic\\manuals.sqlite3"
msgstr "Optional SQLite file used for manual text search. \nExample: %LOCALAPPDATA%\\comsol_mcp\\semantic\\manuals.sqlite3"

msgid "Optional folder containing the local semantic-search model. \nExample: %LOCALAPPDATA%\\comsol_mcp\\semantic\\models"
msgstr "Optional folder containing the local semantic-search model. \nExample: %LOCALAPPDATA%\\comsol_mcp\\semantic\\models"

